tex_4013 = r'''\begin{proposition}[All-Vd0 skeleton-data obstruction]
\label{prop:nplus-zero-all-vd0}
Let the center role be CE1 or CE2. Assume all six vertex roles are Vd0,
\[
 A_i+B_i\le1\qquad(i=0,\ldots,5),
\]
and the seven open roles cover the full skeleton
\[
 S=\partial H\cup\bigcup_{i=0}^5r_i.
\]
Then no such configuration exists. Consequently the same role data cannot
cover all of $H$.
\end{proposition}

\begin{proof}
Let $d_i^C$ be the center reach on $r_i$, measured from $O$, and set
$c_i^C=1-d_i^C$. Since every vertex role is Vd0, no adjacent vertex role has
a positive-length trace on $r_i$; diameter locality excludes nonlocal roles.
Skeleton coverage therefore forces
\[
 C_i\ge c_i^C\qquad(i=0,\ldots,5).
\tag{\(*\)}
\]

Let $\mathrm{gr}$ be the number of positive center traces containing a
nonempty V-gap. Singleton V-gaps are included. The center classification gives
$\mathrm{gr}\in\{0,1,2\}$, with $\mathrm{gr}\le1$ in CE1.

If $\mathrm{gr}=0$, the six open vertex traces cover every boundary edge.
Thus
\[
 B_i>1-A_{i+1}.
\]
Nonsupercriticality and the exact capped transfer give
\[
 A_{i+1}>1-B_i
 \ge\widehat g_{C_i}^{\vee}(A_i)\ge A_i,
\]
which produces the impossible strict cycle
\[
 A_0<A_1<\cdots<A_5<A_0.
\]

Suppose $\mathrm{gr}=1$. Normalize the active trace to
\[
 I_R=\left[\frac{k}{R},W+\delta\right]\subset e_{0,1}
\]
and put
\[
 s=\frac{k}{R},\qquad q=R-\delta.
\]
Gap containment gives $B_0\ge s$ and $A_1\ge q$. The companion edge is
absent or gap-free, so $A_0+B_5\ge1$; since $A_0+B_0\le1$, one has
$B_5\ge s$. By \((*)\),
\[
 C_1\ge1-\frac\delta R,
 \qquad
 C_5\ge1-\frac\alpha W.
\]
The exact one-side endpoint theorem gives
\[
 \widehat g_{1-\alpha/W}(1-s)
 +\widehat g_{1-\delta/R}(1-q)<1.
\]
The three internal V triangles $T_2,T_3,T_4$ lie on a center-free boundary
path. The path budget forces their total boundary contribution above three,
contrary to their three nonsupercritical caps.

If $\mathrm{gr}=2$, the center is CE2. The paired endpoint theorem, together
with \((*)\), gives
\[
 p=W-\alpha,\qquad q=R-\delta,
 \qquad F_{p/W}(p)+F_{q/R}(q)<1.
\]
The same center-free three-V-triangle path gives the contradiction.

The three ranks are exhaustive.
\end{proof}'''

